# Character building

Category: Character. Shared method lives in `.cursor/rules/editorial-review.mdc`. Spoken voice in detail is `.cursor/rules/editorial-dialogue.mdc`.

Read `canon/characters/tsunari.md`, `canon/characters/vram.md`, and the whole of `canon/characters/README.md` before judging. The cast list in any rule is not complete.

## Leads

Tsunari's lie: attachment is a trap; speed and striking first are the only truth. She wants unbound survival and the air keys. She needs a partnership that does not make her property. Her ghost is Year 31 AS, her father, the Mosaic inoculation, Sora, and Doc Mercer. She is a calculating stalker, not a waif and not a quip machine.

Vram's body was built for obedience. Early on, peace feels like humiliation, not tenderness. He becomes a man who can refuse two masters. He is not a soft hero in Part I. Track the change at the act breaks in `canon/plot/story_beats_dual_track.md`. A kindness with no scene that earned it is a finding.

Judge a choice against the dossier. If the page is doing a new character beat on purpose, mark a divergence and say what the old lie would have done instead.

## Embodiment

Appearance, scent, and strain markers come from the dossiers and `canon/world/life/README.md`. Flag a body that changes (eyes, height, wings, claws, beard, hair, clothing contract) and a ability used by the wrong strain. Tsunari is Mutation D. Vram is Mutation S with Mutation G wings.

## Secondaries

Each named person needs a dramatic job. If cutting them changes no choice, say so. Do not merge Cassian, Rook, Toby, and Veda into one squad voice. Caelia's jealousy presses the romance. It does not replace it. The Forger, Malakar, Corvus, Xaevis, Lyraen, Gideon, Chen, Kira, and Boran keep the loyalties in the dossier.

Flag a character who explains their own psychology in a speech, a reversal with no pressure, and a person who vanishes across a part where the breakdown still needs them.